# tiny-chess-01 — 4 KB chess engine

Single-file Python engine (`main.py`, 4,081 bytes) for MakeFun bounty
tiny-chess-01. Python 3.13 stdlib only, deterministic, no model calls.

Design: 120-square board, always White-to-move (board rotates 180 deg
after each move). Immutable positions. Negamax alpha-beta + iterative
deepening, fixed 60,000-node budget (no clock, no randomness).
Quiescence (captures; all replies in check). Move-only transposition
table + MVV ordering. Eval: material + tapered Michniewski PSTs
(pawns/kings tapered; knights/bishops and rooks/queens share tables).
No null-move, LMR, or killers (dropped to fit 4,096 bytes, see
NOTES.md). Promotions queen-only; no en-passant. Never sends an
illegal move.

Run: start the kit env server, then
`MAKEFUN_ENV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080 python3 main.py`.
Think 2–3 s/move (limit 10 s).
